{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>For in booths I caused the children of Israel to dwell.</b> There are those among the Sages, may their memory be for a blessing, who said that they made actual booths for themselves, and there are those who said they were clouds of glory. The opinion of those who say they made actual booths for themselves: because of this we were commanded to make booths like them, so that through the commandment of booths the greatness of Israel's merit in the wilderness might be revealed and made known — that they went with the weight of the men and the women and the little ones in a place where it is not in the nature of man to live, and this is what Scripture testified (Joel 2:20): ״ארץ ציה ושממה״, (Numbers 20:5): ״לא מקום זרע ותאנה וגפן״; and so the prophet said to Israel (Jeremiah 2:31): ״המדבר הייתי לישראל אם ארץ מאפליה״ — he says: I did not show them, to Israel, that they were in the wilderness in a land of darkness, for there, in that place, I prepared for them all their needs and they lacked nothing. And according to this opinion, it is possible that vegetation was brought to them from distant lands by way of traders. The opinion of those who say they were clouds of glory: because they went with a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 13:22): ״לא ימיש עמוד הענן יומם ועמוד האש לילה לפני העם״, and they were surrounded and sheltered from every side by clouds of glory; and this is the principal and correct sense in the plain sense of Scripture. Therefore it says, ״for in booths I caused the children of Israel to dwell, in bringing them out of the land of Egypt״, and they should know to declare this wonder — that these booths were clouds of glory; and as the prophet said (Isaiah 4:5): ״וברא יהוה על כל מכון הר ציון ועל מקראיה ענן יומם ועשן ונגה אש להבה לילה כי על כל כבוד חפה״, and adjacent to it: ״וסכה תהיה לצל יומם מחורב״ — and that is a booth of clouds of glory and kinds of lights for the righteous in the world to come; and concerning it David said (Psalms 27:5): ״כי יצפנני בסכה ביום רעה יסתירני״ etc. — it is written בסכה. And the way of the Kabbalah concerning the commandment of the booth, I shall mention it, with the help of the Blessed Name, at the end of the parashah of Re'eh."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:03.390380846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}